I've released version mvm01a of the "Monk Void Modifier" patch.  It
pretty much just sets things up and lets you know how you are at the
end of game.

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#mvm

Again, this nethack-3.4.3 patch breaks save and bones files (sorry).

DETAILS SPOILER:

The void value is set and maintained for all players, but is only used
by the Monk class.  It's little more right now than a Fibonacci scale
applied against the number of items in your inventory (it's hard to
give stuff up).  The fewer items you have, the better your void score.

It's kind of a compensation for the stuff you could be using if you
carried it around.  On the flip side, if you're carrying too much, it
can be a negative modifier.

I plan to have it affect activities that require some intuition, since
if your mind is occupied with all the nifty stuff you could use, then
your problems start to be seen in terms of just the gear you have.

